Optimal Solution - Uses prefix and suffix maximum arrays to compute trapped rainwater in linear time.
                   At each index, trapped water equals min(max left, max right) minus height—precompute both in linear time.

class Solution {
    public int trap(int[] height) {
        // Length of the elevation map
        int n = height.length;
        // If no bars exist, no water can be trapped
        if (n == 0)  return 0;
        // Arrays to store maximum height to the left and right of each index
        int[] leftMax = new int[n];
        int[] rightMax = new int[n];
        // First element's left max is itself
        leftMax[0] = height[0];
        // Last element's right max is itself
        rightMax[n - 1] = height[n - 1];
        // Fill leftMax array
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            leftMax[i] = Math.max(leftMax[i - 1], height[i]);
        }
        // Fill rightMax array
        for (int i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
            rightMax[i] = Math.max(rightMax[i + 1], height[i]);
        }
        // Calculate total trapped water
        int totalWater = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            // Water at each index = min(leftMax, rightMax) - height
            totalWater += Math.min(leftMax[i], rightMax[i]) - height[i];
        }
        return totalWater;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(n).
